{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Love</b> — imperative form, like אחזו לנו שועלים (catch us the foxes)." "<b>Faithful ones</b> — an adjective, like: פסו אמונים (the faithful have failed)." "<b>Upon the pride</b> — those who remain of the men of pride. And the word לעשות (to do) is to set the causation right, like: וימהר לעשות אותו (and he hastened to do it). And it is possible that גאוה (pride) is defective in its bet [i.e., lacks a prepositional bet], and also the word מעשה (deed) is elided, as if he said: and He repays upon the remnant of the doer of a deed in pride."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:10.235759214Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}